{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.MassEnergyEquivalence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.MassEnergyEquivalence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.massEnergy_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.massEnergy_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/mass-energy-equivalence.lean#L43-L68","doc":"At q = 1 the speed of light diverges, recovering the classical\nlimit where c → ∞ (Galilean regime). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.energy","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/mass-energy-equivalence.lean#L38-L41","doc":"**Energy** of a braid class with mass `m`: 𝔈 = m · c_q². ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:mass-energy","label":"def:mass-energy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/mass-energy-equivalence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.speedOfLightSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.speedOfLightSq","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/mass-energy-equivalence.lean#L33-L36","doc":"The speed of light squared: c_q² = 1/(q-1)². ","signatureChunk":0}]}